From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qmicli,pdc: don't g_free() the mmap'd config file contents

load_config_file_from_string() obtains the config file bytes via
g_mapped_file_get_contents(), which returns a pointer *into* the mmap'd
region owned by the GMappedFile. Calling g_free() on that pointer is an
invalid free: the buffer was never returned by the allocator. On glibc it
happened to be silently tolerated in some cases, but on musl's hardened
mallocng it aborts with SIGSEGV, making `qmicli --pdc-load-config` crash
before the config is uploaded to the modem.

The contents are owned by mapped_file (kept alive via g_mapped_file_ref
into data->mapped_file, and released in the context cleanup); they must
not be freed here.

--- a/src/qmicli/qmicli-pdc.c
+++ b/src/qmicli/qmicli-pdc.c
@@ -1123,7 +1123,6 @@ load_config_file_from_string (const gchar *str)
     file_size = g_mapped_file_get_length (mapped_file);
     hash_size = g_checksum_type_get_length (G_CHECKSUM_SHA1);
     checksum = g_checksum_new (G_CHECKSUM_SHA1);
     g_checksum_update (checksum, file_contents, file_size);
-    g_free (file_contents);

     data = g_slice_new (LoadConfigFileData);
     data->mapped_file = g_mapped_file_ref (mapped_file);
